WEBVTT

1
00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:04.540
We have apprehended a dangerous threat in one of our very own labs, quiet!

2
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:18.600
We believe that this... this monstrosity is the product of illegal genetic experimentation.

3
00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:23.080
What deranged lunatic would create something like this?

4
00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:28.360
I prefer deranged genius, but thank you for the introduction.

5
00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:35.680
Dr. Jamba Dukiba, you were tasked with safely studying biological threats, not creating them.

6
00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:41.480
A threat? Experiment 626 is our Federation's most sophisticated weapon.

7
00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.020
626 is unstoppable.

8
00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.380
Indestructible.

9
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:56.740
And smarter than 100 supercomputers!

10
00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:01.500
I don't want to play anymore! It's an atrocity!

11
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:15.560
Silence! He did not ask to be created. Perhaps if he is so intelligent, he has the capacity to reason.

12
00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:22.940
Experiment 626, show us that there is something inside you that is good.

13
00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.080
Look at that atrocity!

14
00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.240
So naughty!

15
00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.420
I did not teach him that.

16
00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:52.580
You have made our decision easy. He is clearly the flawed product of a deranged mind.

17
00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.760
Dr. Dukiba, your lab will be destroyed.

18
00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:57.920
Okay, just leave me 626.

19
00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.920
And 626 exiled.

20
00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.100
Oh, come on!

21
00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.640
Wait! No, no, no, you can't do that!

22
00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:17.500
Don't get any ideas. These guns are locked under genetic signatures.

23
00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.120
They're not going to shoot anyone but you.

24
00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.940
No! No! No!

25
00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.020
Knock it off! The Federation strictly forbids being gross!

26
00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:38.560
Don't hate me, Sid!

27
00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:46.080
Where is he?

28
00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.520
He's loose on Deck C.

29
00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.720
Now heading for the hall.

30
00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.400
What? He is trying to find the police.

31
00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:00.560
Who's this?

32
00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.340
He uh, he took the red one.

33
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:04.440
Fire at will!

34
00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:16.459
He's in hyperspace.

35
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:17.880
Where will he exit?

36
00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:22.060
In 12 hours, we project he will collide with a planet called Earth.

37
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.160
That's a planet full of water.

38
00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.180
Water increases his molecular density.

39
00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:30.840
He'll become heavy and drown.

40
00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:35.300
And so I think we can all say farewell to 6-2.

41
00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.000
You're kidding.

42
00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.940
Oh what a pickle we've got here.

43
00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.380
If only there was a brilliant genius around to help me catch that monster.

44
00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:49.020
You!

45
00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:51.280
You are the reason we're in this mess.

46
00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.700
And I can get you out of it.

47
00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:55.380
If you release me and get me back to my lab.

48
00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:55.800
Nonsense.

49
00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.020
We'll simply vaporize the planet, Captain.

50
00:04:58.240 --> 00:04:59.560
I'm getting ready, Councilwoman.

51
00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:00.200
Hold it!

52
00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:01.100
Hold everything!

53
00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:01.620
Excuse me.

54
00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:01.900
Sorry.

55
00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:02.400
Excuse me.

56
00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:02.680
Pardon me.

57
00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.020
You can't destroy the planet!

58
00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.040
Aw man.

59
00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:06.380
Uh, who's this?

60
00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:07.340
Agent Pleakley.

61
00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.000
Earth expert.

62
00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:08.980
At your service.

63
00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:09.660
Howdy.

64
00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:11.220
Earth expert.

65
00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:14.600
I'm an expert in that planet's floral, fauna, and fashion.

66
00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.000
Yeah, this outfit screams expert.

67
00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:21.680
Oh yeah, I'm researching an Earth species that's half cow and half boy.

68
00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:22.800
It's very fascinating.

69
00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:23.520
Yes, marvelous.

70
00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:24.360
What's your point?

71
00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.880
Oh, uh, Earth is our protected wildlife reserve.

72
00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:29.220
So you've been using it to rebuild the mosquito population.

73
00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:31.720
Crikey.

74
00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.440
Very well, Dr. Drakema.

75
00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:38.100
You will travel to Earth where you will capture the escaped lab experiment known as 626.

76
00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:40.420
Agent Pleakley, you will be going with him.

77
00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.920
You are deputized to ensure he follows Federation rules.

78
00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:44.520
What?

79
00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:45.820
I don't need a babysitter.

80
00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:48.220
This is all very dangerous and it's quite likely you'll die.

81
00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:48.820
Do you accept?

82
00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:54.240
With every heart in my body, of course I accept.

83
00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.740
I'm going to Earth!

84
00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:56.640
Hey, everyone.

85
00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:57.940
If I may, Grand Councilwoman.

86
00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:58.420
Thank you.

87
00:05:58.600 --> 00:05:58.940
Thank you.

88
00:05:59.020 --> 00:05:59.660
Can I hug you?

89
00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:02.060
Oh, sorry.

90
00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.040
Permission to hug the Grand Councilwoman.

91
00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.380
That's not going to happen.

92
00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:05.780
Of course.

93
00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:06.320
I apologize.

94
00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:08.660
I do not need supervision.

95
00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.100
Permission to hug my new partner.

96
00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:11.420
Brilliant.

97
00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:12.080
Permission granted.

98
00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:12.280
Right.

99
00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:15.120
So what I'm just trying to say is that-

100
00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.080
It would just be better if I went by myself.

101
00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:20.640
Do not let the Earthlings discover your mission or I will be forced to intervene.

102
00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.540
Oh, this is a dream they came.

103
00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.460
I have so much packing to do.

104
00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:26.220
Well, well, well, 626.

105
00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:31.140
What hideous, pathetic planet is caught in your crosshairs?

106
00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.440
I know, right?

107
00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:24.580
So cool.

108
00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.340
They have a festival here.

109
00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:29.060
Are you supposed to be here?

110
00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:31.420
I'm in time for the convention.

111
00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:47.720
Cool.

112
00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:49.400
You're right.

113
00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:50.220
Go, go.

114
00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:51.320
Live your life.

115
00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:52.480
No, no, no, no, no, no.

116
00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:53.540
Hello.

117
00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:54.500
Not again.

118
00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:56.860
They deserve to be free.

119
00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:59.820
I'm going to have to talk to Nani about this.

120
00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:05.860
Sorry.

121
00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:06.600
Sorry.

122
00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.100
Sorry.

123
00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:20.760
Sorry.

124
00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:32.130
Hey, you're gonna be late.

125
00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:33.770
Yeah.

126
00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:38.169
What?

127
00:08:38.169 --> 00:08:39.450
Is she? She's always late.

128
00:08:39.549 --> 00:08:40.370
You haven't seen Lilo.

129
00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:49.770
Lilo, thank goodness. I thought you were going to be on time today.

130
00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.930
I had to get a sandwich for Pudge.

131
00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:54.090
Is Pudge a friend in need?

132
00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:56.250
He's a fish. I forgot to tell you that.

133
00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:58.590
So you're late because you fed a sandwich to a fish.

134
00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:00.570
Yeah, Pudge controls the weather.

135
00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:02.710
She's so weird.

136
00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.430
Lilo, honey, come on. Get dressed, honey.

137
00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:10.890
Oh, guys, look. I got a friendship bracelet, too.

138
00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:13.870
That's not a friendship bracelet.

139
00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:16.770
Ew. Garbage girl puts garbage on her arm.

140
00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.490
Girls, come on. Come on.

141
00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.250
You know, silly.

142
00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:24.490
It's not a friendship bracelet if you don't have any friends.

143
00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:25.810
Girls, girls, girls. Wait.

144
00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:27.490
Quickly, quickly. Stand in line. Get ready.

145
00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:41.850
No.

146
00:09:56.650 --> 00:10:01.250
No, no, no, no.

147
00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:03.910
She's not coming.

148
00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:15.940
Hey Wolf, can you put those in the door?

149
00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:17.680
Read the note!

150
00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.820
I'm sorry, I just dropped it over there, okay?

151
00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:22.880
How about drug guidance?

152
00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:25.900
Mom, that must be so stressful for you.

153
00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.380
How about you just leave me alone to die?

154
00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:30.900
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

155
00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:01.620
Use the back.

156
00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:04.100
It's just about right in the back.

157
00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:16.220
These little houses, right?

158
00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:18.420
You just gotta have a good...

159
00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:19.260
Oh.

160
00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:22.020
There you go.

161
00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:25.820
Um, actually, would you mind waiting here for just a second?

162
00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:26.880
Yes, of course.

163
00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:27.300
Okay.

164
00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:35.460
So, uh, what can I get you to drink?

165
00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:36.860
Do you have tea?

166
00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.060
Of course I have.

167
00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:42.280
There's a lot of unpaid bills here, Nani.

168
00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:48.180
How often would you say you leave your little sister home alone?

169
00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:48.900
What?

170
00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.120
No, why would I do that?

171
00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.240
I would never leave my sister home alone.

172
00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:57.920
Smoke, Nani!

173
00:12:58.840 --> 00:12:59.860
Oh, oh, oh!

174
00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:00.800
The alarm!

175
00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:01.700
The smoke alarm!

176
00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.140
Oh, don't worry.

177
00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:04.640
There's no batteries in there.

178
00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:05.440
Lilo!

179
00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.740
They took mine because it kept going off.

180
00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:08.600
That's not true.

181
00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.300
Say aloha to Mrs. Kekoa.

182
00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:15.040
Aloha, Lilo.

183
00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:16.440
How are you?

184
00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:18.020
Is that blood?

185
00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:20.520
Oh, yeah.

186
00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.220
I've been practicing jumping out of my window.

187
00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:24.820
Ha, she's kidding.

188
00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:29.280
She's actually been very well behaved recently, haven't you?

189
00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:29.620
Right?

190
00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:32.120
Yeah.

191
00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:35.760
I've been more than good, Mrs. Kekoa.

192
00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:39.960
I've been doing really, really great at hula.

193
00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:46.060
Made a ton of new friends there, and they all think I'm the coolest.

194
00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:52.220
I've been eating a lot of organic stuff.

195
00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:53.200
Sometimes I'm not.

196
00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:59.260
Sometimes I eat too much, and I've been eating five or ten times a day.

197
00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:04.860
Sometimes I eat so much I can't breathe.

198
00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:08.820
That's enough imagination for you, you little weirdy.

199
00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:10.300
Oh, tea's ready.

200
00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.530
Mmm, okay, pretty sweet.

201
00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:25.650
Okay, Nani, we both know this didn't go well today.

202
00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:31.610
I can see you're trying, but you're too smart for me to beat around the bush here.

203
00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:35.490
I know it hasn't been that long since your parents passed away,

204
00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:39.750
but my job is to make sure that Lilo is in a stable environment.

205
00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:43.370
And I can't say that in good conscience right now.

206
00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:48.590
Listen, I know this is a lot, but you're practically a kid yourself.

207
00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:00.800
Look, you seem like a goal-oriented person.

208
00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:04.320
We have a new director coming into town next week.

209
00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:08.480
And I would really, really love to tell him that you girls have turned the corner.

210
00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:11.260
So why don't we come up with some goals to achieve by then?

211
00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:12.200
Yeah, yeah.

212
00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:13.380
Here.

213
00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:18.670
Three things.

214
00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:24.710
First, I want this house cleaned, including laundry and a fully stocked fridge.

215
00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:25.990
Perfect.

216
00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:29.130
Second, pay all those bills I saw in the kitchen.

217
00:15:30.170 --> 00:15:30.530
Yes.

218
00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:34.650
And third, file for health insurance for you and Lilo.

219
00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:35.910
Got it.

220
00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:40.890
Now, if you do those three things by Friday, I might be able to give you some more time.

221
00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.170
Thank you.

222
00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:48.230
What's capri-sagna?

223
00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:50.290
Yeah, I take it.

224
00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.830
And also get the insurance.

225
00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:56.410
Yeah, yeah, you got it.

226
00:15:56.730 --> 00:16:00.690
You're gonna need that health insurance for when I kill you!

227
00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:08.730
Holy cow!

228
00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:10.550
You're gonna smuggle our batteries!

229
00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:12.290
I'll show you capri-sagna!

230
00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:15.010
Look at me!

231
00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:21.970
Why didn't you wait at Hula?

232
00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:23.630
Because you weren't there!

233
00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:24.870
Do you want them to split us up?

234
00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:27.130
Because that's what's gonna happen if we don't get it together!

235
00:16:28.390 --> 00:16:28.830
Hey!

236
00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.910
Stop pretending you're my mom!

237
00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:34.930
Oh, at least I don't tell the social worker I like dumping out a window!

238
00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:37.110
Much better than listening to you!

239
00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:38.150
No, you're a prude!

240
00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:39.970
I know you're my mom!

241
00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:41.690
Woo-hoo!

242
00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:46.270
Hey, Albert!

243
00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:56.450
There she is, Miss Aloha!

244
00:16:57.290 --> 00:16:58.430
Yeah, not today.

245
00:16:58.690 --> 00:16:59.390
She's not.

246
00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:00.570
Meaning it'll never go well.

247
00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:03.470
I never liked that government lady anyway.

248
00:17:03.849 --> 00:17:05.510
Why is she always so smiley?

249
00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:06.910
Give me the creeps!

250
00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:08.430
Yeah, well, our future's in her hands.

251
00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:09.829
Ah, no, no, no.

252
00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:12.030
Your future is in your hands.

253
00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:14.069
And you're gonna have a very bright future

254
00:17:14.069 --> 00:17:15.569
because of that Akamai brand of yours.

255
00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:19.310
What?

256
00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:22.270
Your acceptance letter to your dream school

257
00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:24.290
magically taken out of your trash

258
00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.349
and appearing in your bag at your place of work?

259
00:17:26.589 --> 00:17:28.250
Ooh, that's a sign, girl!

260
00:17:28.370 --> 00:17:29.370
Will you stop with this?

261
00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:31.490
That school is the best school in the whole world

262
00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:32.610
for that bionic magnet!

263
00:17:32.870 --> 00:17:33.250
Bionic?

264
00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:34.750
Marine biology.

265
00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:35.850
Marine biology!

266
00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:39.430
And they already let you in once

267
00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:41.670
and they wanted to keep you for a full ride.

268
00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:43.670
Yeah, I know, but Tutu, there's no way.

269
00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:44.910
Lilo needs me here.

270
00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:46.850
You ever ask Lilo what she wants?

271
00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.270
She's six, so no.

272
00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:50.190
