He's not a puppy, Lilo. I'm not even sure if it's a dog.

854
00:47:34.360 --> 00:47:34.520
Look!

855
00:47:43.120 --> 00:47:44.000
Get down!

856
00:47:44.160 --> 00:47:44.940
Gage! Stop!

857
00:47:45.600 --> 00:47:47.160
Quiet! We're taking him back!

858
00:47:47.660 --> 00:47:49.440
First thing tomorrow morning!

859
00:47:52.040 --> 00:47:53.220
Why are you so strong?

860
00:47:53.540 --> 00:47:54.940
But I worked for him!

861
00:47:55.080 --> 00:47:56.060
And it came true!

862
00:47:56.180 --> 00:47:58.020
We said one day! That was our deal!

863
00:47:58.120 --> 00:48:00.000
What does that say? On the fridge reader!

864
00:48:00.100 --> 00:48:01.480
We are not keeping this thing!

865
00:48:01.520 --> 00:48:02.860
Ohana means family.

866
00:48:02.860 --> 00:48:05.880
Family means nobody gets left behind or...

867
00:48:05.880 --> 00:48:06.820
Or forgotten!

868
00:48:18.270 --> 00:48:21.270
Why are you trying to go against your mama and papa then?

869
00:48:21.310 --> 00:48:22.650
Because we were left behind!

870
00:48:25.000 --> 00:48:25.240
Look.

871
00:48:26.980 --> 00:48:27.880
I know.

872
00:48:28.460 --> 00:48:30.560
All that stuff sounds so nice.

873
00:48:31.120 --> 00:48:32.560
It sounds really nice to me too.

874
00:48:32.660 --> 00:48:34.040
But that is not reality.

875
00:48:35.060 --> 00:48:36.340
This is reality.

876
00:48:37.100 --> 00:48:39.160
And I need you to start living in it.

877
00:48:39.460 --> 00:48:40.120
With me.

878
00:48:43.580 --> 00:48:45.780
Look, can you just get control of your dog?

879
00:48:48.600 --> 00:48:51.560
And I don't even want to think about what social services it's going to be.

880
00:48:55.070 --> 00:48:56.890
Ace, Foster, get me the social worker.

881
00:48:57.330 --> 00:48:58.130
I'm going undercover.

882
00:49:00.070 --> 00:49:02.710
You've got to stop causing problems, Gage.

883
00:49:03.710 --> 00:49:06.470
You can play with squirrels, but be nice.

884
00:49:06.750 --> 00:49:08.510
She was my best friend before you.

885
00:49:08.810 --> 00:49:09.590
Hey, stop!

886
00:49:10.350 --> 00:49:11.850
Bad dog! Bad dog!

887
00:49:12.350 --> 00:49:13.930
Don't pull on her head!

888
00:49:15.290 --> 00:49:17.230
She's recovering from her surgery.

889
00:49:20.450 --> 00:49:22.250
Hey, that's my favorite phone!

890
00:49:22.830 --> 00:49:23.430
Stop it!

891
00:49:26.510 --> 00:49:27.950
This is called rule, okay?

892
00:49:28.170 --> 00:49:30.770
That means I'm free, so I won't ever touch this!

893
00:49:30.770 --> 00:49:32.810
Now be good!

894
00:49:35.310 --> 00:49:38.250
Be good for one second.

895
00:49:44.290 --> 00:49:47.810
She was smartest in her whole class.

896
00:49:52.600 --> 00:49:53.740
That's the board.

897
00:49:54.380 --> 00:49:55.820
That's how you serve.

898
00:49:57.780 --> 00:49:59.620
Oh, this is how she trained.

899
00:50:00.180 --> 00:50:01.640
She was great at it.

900
00:50:01.640 --> 00:50:05.680
And she had a whole room full of witch rofies.

901
00:50:08.640 --> 00:50:11.380
We used to go to the beach all the time.

902
00:50:11.960 --> 00:50:13.020
She used to be fun.

903
00:50:13.940 --> 00:50:15.220
But she couldn't hurt them.

904
00:50:18.860 --> 00:50:20.780
I don't think you're supposed to drink that.

905
00:50:25.080 --> 00:50:26.420
Did you have a family?

906
00:50:28.960 --> 00:50:29.480
Family?

907
00:50:33.560 --> 00:50:34.280
Family.

908
00:50:34.760 --> 00:50:35.460
That's close.

909
00:50:36.340 --> 00:50:37.700
Like mom and papa.

910
00:50:38.240 --> 00:50:43.380
The people at home who give you lots of hugs and kisses and are there for you.

911
00:50:43.980 --> 00:50:45.080
Even when...

912
00:50:45.960 --> 00:50:46.680
No.

913
00:50:47.460 --> 00:50:49.060
No family.

914
00:50:51.160 --> 00:50:53.480
Is that why you act bad sometimes?

915
00:50:54.720 --> 00:50:55.620
That's okay.

916
00:50:56.380 --> 00:50:58.480
Maybe my parents talk to your parents.

917
00:50:58.900 --> 00:51:00.120
And they say yes to each other.

918
00:51:01.020 --> 00:51:01.280
Huh?

919
00:51:02.880 --> 00:51:03.180
Tessa.

920
00:51:04.500 --> 00:51:05.440
Hey, hey, what's up?

921
00:51:06.260 --> 00:51:07.480
Oh, that's hula.

922
00:51:08.000 --> 00:51:08.840
What's hula?

923
00:51:09.160 --> 00:51:10.380
It's a Hawaiian dance.

924
00:51:10.920 --> 00:51:11.680
You want to try?

925
00:51:14.130 --> 00:51:15.110
Come on, come on, come on.

926
00:51:15.650 --> 00:51:17.370
Now follow what I do.

927
00:51:22.720 --> 00:51:23.920
Aloha ooa.

928
00:51:26.140 --> 00:51:27.340
Aloha ooa.

929
00:51:27.340 --> 00:51:31.860
Well, I can't own a home, I know.

930
00:51:32.460 --> 00:51:38.240
It can't wait for one fine day.

931
00:51:39.080 --> 00:51:42.460
I hope we are young.

932
00:51:43.460 --> 00:51:49.540
Until we meet again.

933
00:52:00.580 --> 00:52:03.360
I'm so glad I found you.

934
00:52:04.600 --> 00:52:05.980
Can I kiss your nose?

935
00:52:17.250 --> 00:52:18.410
Noni, Noni.

936
00:52:19.010 --> 00:52:20.530
You have to see this.

937
00:52:21.110 --> 00:52:22.910
Okay, just like we practiced.

938
00:52:24.250 --> 00:52:24.850
What are you doing?

939
00:52:25.410 --> 00:52:26.070
What is this?

940
00:52:28.650 --> 00:52:29.630
I'm excited.

941
00:52:30.390 --> 00:52:31.710
Come, I want you.

942
00:52:38.980 --> 00:52:40.700
I love that song.

943
00:52:41.060 --> 00:52:43.380
Can you even see?

944
00:52:43.940 --> 00:52:45.480
Oh, we're gonna be late.

945
00:52:48.940 --> 00:52:50.100
Come on, turn that off.

946
00:52:50.180 --> 00:52:50.680
Go get your shoes.

947
00:52:51.040 --> 00:52:51.980
That's my superpower.

948
00:52:52.480 --> 00:52:57.080
The only superpower that I have is sometimes when I run too fast, I fart.

949
00:52:57.080 --> 00:53:01.140
Aloha ooa.

950
00:53:01.140 --> 00:53:01.940
Nice to meet you.

951
00:53:02.280 --> 00:53:05.160
I appreciate someone with your seniority coming to help us.

952
00:53:05.300 --> 00:53:06.880
Well, this is my top priority.

953
00:53:08.440 --> 00:53:09.200
Okay, come on.

954
00:53:09.540 --> 00:53:11.060
Let's go, let's go.

955
00:53:11.520 --> 00:53:13.080
Hurry up, we're already late.

956
00:53:13.220 --> 00:53:14.000
We gotta go.

957
00:53:15.860 --> 00:53:18.360
This is our social services director.

958
00:53:19.280 --> 00:53:19.540
Hello.

959
00:53:19.740 --> 00:53:20.040
Hi.

960
00:53:20.960 --> 00:53:24.020
I thought you weren't coming in until next week.

961
00:53:24.140 --> 00:53:26.480
No, Noni, your case has been elevated.

962
00:53:26.480 --> 00:53:28.660
So, this is Lila.

963
00:53:28.980 --> 00:53:31.320
And who is this little friend?

964
00:53:31.580 --> 00:53:32.520
That's my new dog.

965
00:53:32.540 --> 00:53:34.440
Noni, I heard what happened last night.

966
00:53:34.660 --> 00:53:35.500
Can we talk for a second?

967
00:53:36.760 --> 00:53:38.000
Yeah, sure.

968
00:53:38.660 --> 00:53:39.680
Because I was sick.

969
00:53:39.840 --> 00:53:40.540
Oh, really?

970
00:53:40.920 --> 00:53:41.560
What was happening?

971
00:53:41.600 --> 00:53:43.140
You look very sick right now.

972
00:53:43.260 --> 00:53:43.780
That's all I'm saying.

973
00:53:44.120 --> 00:53:54.440
You don't look like a social worker.

974
00:53:55.100 --> 00:53:56.500
I'm a special brain.

975
00:53:57.120 --> 00:53:58.100
Your neck looks like clover.

976
00:53:58.720 --> 00:53:59.560
You can read, huh?

977
00:53:59.700 --> 00:54:00.580
Yeah, I can read.

978
00:54:01.060 --> 00:54:02.480
I'm reading you like a book.

979
00:54:03.400 --> 00:54:04.780
That's true, I'll get health insurance.

980
00:54:05.040 --> 00:54:06.000
Don't even worry about it.

981
00:54:06.060 --> 00:54:07.400
You said I had it until the end of the week, right?

982
00:54:07.600 --> 00:54:09.900
Lila, bitch, let's go find a job.

983
00:54:12.300 --> 00:54:12.700
Gotcha.

984
00:54:13.440 --> 00:54:15.760
But I do want to know a little bit more about you.

985
00:54:16.760 --> 00:54:18.580
Okay, what would you like to know about me, please?

986
00:54:18.920 --> 00:54:20.120
Where did you get the name Jennifer?

987
00:54:21.020 --> 00:54:22.180
It's a family name.

988
00:54:23.880 --> 00:54:24.920
Are you kidding me?

989
00:54:30.360 --> 00:54:31.520
Let's go, let's go, let's go.

990
00:54:32.300 --> 00:54:33.480
We have to catch him today.

991
00:54:34.160 --> 00:54:36.820
Why did you choose this foolish method of transportation?

992
00:54:37.040 --> 00:54:37.760
Hurry, go for it.

993
00:54:40.890 --> 00:54:42.150
Okay, this is it, Lila.

994
00:54:42.530 --> 00:54:43.830
Okay, this is our last shot.

995
00:54:44.490 --> 00:54:45.870
If I don't find a job by today,

996
00:54:47.630 --> 00:54:49.250
then we are going to be separated.

997
00:54:51.390 --> 00:54:52.190
Hey, listen.

998
00:54:52.830 --> 00:54:53.290
For real.

999
00:54:54.690 --> 00:54:58.130
I need you and him to be on your best behavior.

1000
00:54:58.350 --> 00:54:58.830
Okay?

1001
00:55:01.610 --> 00:55:03.150
Okay, good luck.

1002
00:55:07.360 --> 00:55:08.280
Okay, Stitch.

1003
00:55:08.480 --> 00:55:10.080
Mommy is counting on us.

1004
00:55:10.200 --> 00:55:11.300
So let's get to work.

1005
00:55:11.540 --> 00:55:12.000
Ready?

1006
00:55:12.620 --> 00:55:12.960
Stitch.

1007
00:55:19.880 --> 00:55:21.080
Okay, class.

1008
00:55:21.300 --> 00:55:21.980
Listen up.

1009
00:55:22.280 --> 00:55:23.780
This is your badness level.

1010
00:55:24.040 --> 00:55:26.460
It's unusually high for someone your size.

1011
00:55:26.460 --> 00:55:27.760
But we'll fix that.

1012
00:55:27.960 --> 00:55:29.340
So lesson number one.

1013
00:55:29.660 --> 00:55:31.400
Lend a helping hand.

1014
00:55:31.740 --> 00:55:32.980
Or a paw.

1015
00:55:33.620 --> 00:55:35.140
So this is how you clean.

1016
00:55:35.480 --> 00:55:36.740
First, use this.

1017
00:55:37.780 --> 00:55:38.880
Okay, we gotta get closer.

1018
00:55:39.320 --> 00:55:39.580
Okay.

1019
00:55:43.040 --> 00:55:43.560
That's better.

1020
00:55:44.220 --> 00:55:45.440
Lesson number two.

1021
00:55:45.580 --> 00:55:46.620
Don't wreck stuff.

1022
00:55:46.760 --> 00:55:47.740
It's really fragile.

1023
00:55:48.020 --> 00:55:50.380
So, can't break it every time you sneeze.

1024
00:55:51.780 --> 00:55:53.080
Now, your turn.

1025
00:55:56.780 --> 00:55:57.120
Really?

1026
00:56:00.500 --> 00:56:01.280
You can't just say,

1027
00:56:01.400 --> 00:56:02.740
Hey, let's get scooters and that's the plan.

1028
00:56:02.880 --> 00:56:03.600
At the nine-to-five.

1029
00:56:07.180 --> 00:56:08.760
Can you tell me how you did it?

1030
00:56:08.820 --> 00:56:09.460
I have no idea.

1031
00:56:09.540 --> 00:56:10.240
I looked at the light.

1032
00:56:10.600 --> 00:56:11.280
Lesson three.

1033
00:56:12.460 --> 00:56:13.440
Make a mess.

1034
00:56:17.520 --> 00:56:18.400
There's that one.

1035
00:56:22.420 --> 00:56:23.100
Now, okay.

1036
00:56:24.680 --> 00:56:25.020
Okay.

1037
00:56:25.020 --> 00:56:25.800
Okay.

1038
00:56:26.460 --> 00:56:26.960
Good job.

1039
00:56:32.820 --> 00:56:34.960
How did it go?

1040
00:56:37.960 --> 00:56:39.340
Now look at this hotel.

1041
00:56:39.620 --> 00:56:39.900
Wait.

1042
00:56:40.280 --> 00:56:41.280
Well, um.

1043
00:56:41.280 --> 00:56:41.620
Hmm.

1044
00:56:54.960 --> 00:56:55.560
Okay.

1045
00:56:58.680 --> 00:57:00.280
Maybe you can do something you love.

1046
00:57:11.900 --> 00:57:13.180
Go, go, go.

1047
00:57:13.380 --> 00:57:14.240
And, punch.

1048
00:59:39.980 --> 00:59:45.660
Code 51. I repeat, code 51. Send an extraction team now.

1049
00:59:45.840 --> 00:59:48.100
Cobra, my hands are tied until the sample is processed.

1050
00:59:49.020 --> 00:59:52.519
Someone's after it too. The next chance I get, I'm catching it.

1051
00:59:52.880 --> 00:59:57.160
Stevie, help, help.

1052
00:59:57.620 --> 00:59:58.480
Lilo, can you hear me?

1053
01:00:01.680 --> 01:00:02.680
Call an ambulance!

1054
01:00:12.780 --> 01:00:18.560
Well folks, she asked if she could ride in the MRI machine. I told her I would check with you.

1055
01:00:20.300 --> 01:00:21.220
She's fun.

1056
01:00:23.020 --> 01:00:29.360
She got lucky. A few more seconds it could have been much worse, but overall...

1057
01:00:29.920 --> 01:00:31.940
It's a service animal.

1058
01:00:32.900 --> 01:00:37.320
Okay. And you can see the front and they'll run your insurance. Okay?

1059
01:00:39.260 --> 01:00:39.760
Mahalo.

1060
01:00:41.980 --> 01:00:43.880
Uh-oh. What?

1061
01:00:45.240 --> 01:00:48.680
No, no, absolutely not. It's not just the bills, Nani.

1062
01:00:49.800 --> 01:00:52.300
It's time for you to think about what's best for Lilo.

1063
01:00:55.220 --> 01:00:58.220
There's a way that the state will pay for all of this.

1064
01:01:01.240 --> 01:01:07.960
But it means that you have to officially relinquish guardianship of Lilo.

1065
01:01:09.900 --> 01:01:13.440
What would that look like?

1066
01:01:15.000 --> 01:01:18.680
Well, we take our lead from you.

1067
01:01:20.160 --> 01:01:22.300
You tell us how you want to proceed.

1068
01:01:43.420 --> 01:01:44.460
Say goodbye.

1069
01:01:45.260 --> 01:01:48.880
No. We don't say goodbye.

1070
01:01:50.300 --> 01:01:52.260
We say a hui hou.

1071
01:01:53.920 --> 01:01:55.620
Until we meet again.

1072
01:02:03.400 --> 01:02:04.920
I really thought they could make it work.

1073
01:02:08.420 --> 01:02:10.240
Why would he protect her like that?

1074
01:02:10.280 --> 01:02:12.120
You don't think they're kind of cute together, though?

1075
01:02:12.120 --> 01:02:15.160
No, he's not a pet. He's an experiment and a dangerous one at that.

1076
01:02:15.260 --> 01:02:17.740
I just think he's a lot cuter than you think he is dangerous.

1077
01:02:17.980 --> 01:02:21.000
He has sharp teeth, he has claws. I designed him to be dangerous.

1078
01:02:21.120 --> 01:02:21.900
Dangerous teeth?

1079
01:02:23.360 --> 01:02:24.500
You gotta answer that.

1080
01:02:26.220 --> 01:02:26.880
Don't answer that.

1081
01:02:28.960 --> 01:02:30.340
Quickly. For me.

1082
01:02:31.820 --> 01:02:34.680
Your Ma'am's the agent we got here not ignoring your calls.

1083
01:02:34.840 --> 01:02:38.640
We just intercepted a call from human authorities. Do you realize what you have done?

1084
01:02:38.960 --> 01:02:39.240
Nope.

1085
01:02:39.620 --> 01:02:41.820
Play the recording and take off that ridiculous hat.

1086
01:02:42.540 --> 01:02:44.940
Code 51. We found them.

1087
01:02:45.860 --> 01:02:46.400
Take them.

1088
01:02:46.760 --> 01:02:51.780
And not only have you alerted the humans to our existence, but you still haven't captured 626.

1089
01:02:52.420 --> 01:02:55.760
Grand Captain Woman, with all due respect, I'm not sure you know what's going on with 626.

1090
01:02:55.940 --> 01:03:02.480
We have found a glitch, which is making it a little harder to get him off this planet.

1091
01:03:02.580 --> 01:03:05.060
But don't worry, I'm sure I can figure out...

1092
01:03:05.060 --> 01:03:07.000
You're a glitch, you buffoon.

1093
01:03:07.000 --> 01:03:10.500
I have had enough, Dr. Dukley, but you have exhausted my patience.

1094
01:03:10.800 --> 01:03:12.660
Consider our deal terminated.

1095
01:03:13.100 --> 01:03:13.620
What?

1096
01:03:13.840 --> 01:03:15.060
No tantrums.

1097
01:03:15.240 --> 01:03:18.960
Agent Peatley is hereby deputized to detain you under Federation orders

1098
01:03:18.960 --> 01:03:21.680
and escort you back to Turo immediately.

1099
01:03:22.940 --> 01:03:23.780
Uh, hello?

1100
01:03:24.260 --> 01:03:25.320
Oh, now? Right now?

1101
01:03:25.520 --> 01:03:26.740
No, later. What do you think?

1102
01:03:26.780 --> 01:03:27.660
No, no, no.

1103
01:03:27.720 --> 01:03:32.700
This is not a debate. A Federation detail is on its way to clean up your mess.

1104
01:03:33.380 --> 01:03:34.620
Did she hang up?

1105
01:03:36.660 --> 01:03:37.180
Jumba?

1106
01:03:38.260 --> 01:03:42.060
Well, Federation has always kind of been my way, overreacting all the time.

1107
01:03:42.520 --> 01:03:45.620
But, work's work, and we've got Apollo orders, and...

1108
01:03:46.620 --> 01:03:46.860
What?

1109
01:03:47.480 --> 01:03:48.920
Aloha, and Mahalo.

1110
01:03:49.440 --> 01:03:50.380
Oh, you're learning fast.

1111
01:03:56.180 --> 01:03:58.400
I really thought we were getting closer.

1112
01:03:58.780 --> 01:04:00.460
It's time to do this my way.

1113
01:04:02.720 --> 01:04:03.100
Oh, no.

1114
01:04:05.240 --> 01:04:06.660
Hey, Boopfang.

1115
01:04:07.560 --> 01:04:07.900
Hey.

1116
01:04:08.820 --> 01:04:10.000
What are you doing, silly?

1117
01:04:10.540 --> 01:04:14.680
Oh, just playing with my doll that I made at Tutu.

1118
01:04:15.180 --> 01:04:16.040
Aw, cute.

1119
01:04:16.420 --> 01:04:17.080
Pizza.

1120
01:04:21.740 --> 01:04:26.820
So, remember that time that I went to the North Shore that one summer?

1121
01:04:27.560 --> 01:04:27.940
Yeah.

1122
01:04:27.940 --> 01:04:35.960
And we were on opposite sides of the island, but we could, you know, go and visit anytime we wanted, right?

1123
01:04:36.080 --> 01:04:39.080
We just weren't together all the time.

1124
01:04:39.440 --> 01:04:40.520
But we could call.

1125
01:04:41.300 --> 01:04:47.000
You would tell me about all of your fun little adventures with Alvin and Tutu and stuff like that.

1126
01:04:47.480 --> 01:04:51.760
And we could talk a lot, just not all the time.

1127
01:04:55.800 --> 01:04:56.880
Is this connecting at all?

1128
01:04:58.120 --> 01:05:00.500
You're going back to the 15th?

1129
01:05:01.400 --> 01:05:02.820
No, no.

1130
01:05:04.300 --> 01:05:10.880
It's just that with Stitch and everything this week, things have gone from bad to worse, so...

1131
01:05:12.780 --> 01:05:14.240
We're going to have to make some changes.

1132
01:05:17.120 --> 01:05:17.680
And...

1133
01:05:22.580 --> 01:05:26.060
You know, I have to get some air.

1134
01:05:31.810 --> 01:05:32.450
Hey.

1135
01:05:51.360 --> 01:05:54.560
Remember when Papa took us camping out here?

1136
01:05:55.880 --> 01:05:56.180
What?

1137
01:05:56.340 --> 01:05:58.700
Yeah, remember? I had s'mores.

1138
01:05:59.100 --> 01:06:00.600
And you also did too.

1139
01:06:01.040 --> 01:06:02.200
Mama didn't take us camping.

1140
01:06:03.200 --> 01:06:05.120
They were fumigating. We had termites.

1141
01:06:06.100 --> 01:06:07.500
I went camping.

1142
01:06:08.200 --> 01:06:08.880
We had fun.

1143
01:06:14.450 --> 01:06:16.130
They were really good parents.

1144
01:06:17.410 --> 01:06:17.950
Hey.

1145
01:06:18.610 --> 01:06:20.070
I changed my mind.

1146
01:06:21.530 --> 01:06:22.610
What's that?

1147
01:06:25.150 --> 01:06:27.510
I'm making it with Mom too.

1148
01:06:36.920 --> 01:06:38.580
Come on, do it.

1149
01:06:39.100 --> 01:06:39.500
Me?

1150
01:07:35.320 --> 01:07:44.660
Ike ona ona noho i ka lipo

1151
01:07:44.660 --> 01:07:49.680
Wai fa'a dem place

1152
01:07:49.680 --> 01:07:54.040
A hoia e o

1153
01:07:54.040 --> 01:08:01.140
Until we meet again

1154
01:08:11.430 --> 01:08:13.709
I want you to know...

1155
01:08:15.540 --> 01:08:17.200
I love you very much.

1156
01:09:21.760 --> 01:09:22.820
It's going to be okay.

1157
01:09:24.200 --> 01:09:24.860
I promise.

1158
01:09:47.000 --> 01:09:48.020
She's not here.

1159
01:09:49.120 --> 01:09:50.320
What do you mean she's not here?

1160
01:09:51.680 --> 01:09:54.160
I don't know. Maybe she's at the neighbor's house.

1161
01:09:58.600 --> 01:10:00.780
Wake up.

1162
01:10:08.320 --> 01:10:08.900
Stitch!

1163
01:10:16.000 --> 01:10:17.460
Stitch?

1164
01:10:18.440 --> 01:10:19.800
Stitch!

1165
01:10:20.540 --> 01:10:22.260
I thought I lost you.

1166
01:10:23.820 --> 01:10:25.520
Stitch break.

1167
01:10:26.280 --> 01:10:27.140
Fabulous.

1168
01:10:28.440 --> 01:10:29.520
It was an accident.

1169
01:10:30.480 --> 01:10:31.540
Like I messed up.

1170
01:10:32.620 --> 01:10:34.680
But Stitch...

1171
01:10:38.280 --> 01:10:43.800
I'm bad. Stitch is bad.

1172
01:10:45.260 --> 01:10:46.120
You're not bad.

1173
01:10:47.020 --> 01:10:49.980
You just do bad things sometimes.

1174
01:10:51.100 --> 01:10:52.840
Ohano means family.

1175
01:10:54.820 --> 01:10:58.340
Sometimes family isn't perfect.

1176
01:11:05.140 --> 01:11:10.780
But that doesn't mean they aren't good.

1177
01:11:12.840 --> 01:11:13.660
Excuse me.

1178
01:11:24.660 --> 01:11:28.880
I'm here to help. This animal belongs to me.

1179
01:11:29.140 --> 01:11:31.420
She's not an animal. She's my friend.

1180
01:11:32.800 --> 01:11:34.120
Do you have anything else to say?

1181
01:11:39.660 --> 01:11:40.460
Hand me that.

1182
01:11:41.240 --> 01:11:43.700
You're going to use it. I'm going to count to three.

1183
01:11:44.000 --> 01:11:45.120
And then I want you to drop it.

1184
01:11:45.800 --> 01:11:46.240
One.

1185
01:11:48.980 --> 01:11:49.420
Two.

1186
01:11:51.920 --> 01:11:52.360
One.

1187
01:11:56.620 --> 01:11:56.720
Two.

1188
01:11:56.720 --> 01:11:57.200
Four.

1189
01:11:57.960 --> 01:11:59.660
You're a genius, Stitch.

1190
01:11:59.900 --> 01:12:02.420
I'm not a genius.

1191
01:12:03.740 --> 01:12:07.080
First rule, a stranger's danger is my animal.

1192
01:12:08.160 --> 01:12:08.520
Nani?

1193
01:12:10.100 --> 01:12:10.980
Nani?

1194
01:12:12.140 --> 01:12:12.620
Lilo!

1195
01:12:13.240 --> 01:12:13.660
Lilo!

1196
01:12:14.740 --> 01:12:16.260
This is all my fault.

1197
01:12:20.820 --> 01:12:21.700
Hoy!

1198
01:12:32.220 --> 01:12:32.680
Hoy!

1199
01:12:37.180 --> 01:12:38.780
And now I have a weapon.

1200
01:12:39.840 --> 01:12:41.880
Wait, why would I know what your sister eats?

1201
01:12:41.980 --> 01:12:44.400
I don't know. This is the only phone number I could find.

1202
01:12:45.480 --> 01:12:47.000
Good night. She's back.

1203
01:12:47.580 --> 01:12:47.980
Nani!

1204
01:12:52.020 --> 01:12:52.480
Nani!

1205
01:12:52.480 --> 01:12:53.700
Stitch, no!

1206
01:13:04.220 --> 01:13:09.160
Okay, 626. Very clever trick.

1207
01:13:09.460 --> 01:13:11.340
Funny. I got to stare at my own derriere.

1208
01:13:11.700 --> 01:13:13.440
I've always wanted to do that.

1209
01:13:13.480 --> 01:13:13.720
What are you doing?

1210
01:13:17.900 --> 01:13:23.300
Okay, listen, I just want to say the Federation doesn't exactly appreciate...

1211
01:13:27.180 --> 01:13:29.780
I know you're in there.

1212
01:13:30.120 --> 01:13:31.540
Come out, please.

1213
01:13:31.640 --> 01:13:33.560
I've got huge plans for you.

1214
01:13:33.800 --> 01:13:34.640
I mean, for us.

1215
01:13:39.140 --> 01:13:41.060
Go away, hairy potato!

1216
01:13:42.000 --> 01:13:43.520
Did you just call me a hairy potato?

1217
01:13:43.980 --> 01:13:44.800
That's not nice.

1218
01:13:45.880 --> 01:13:46.960
Bring it, bring it, bring it!

1219
01:13:49.560 --> 01:13:50.680
Come back!

1220
01:13:51.220 --> 01:13:52.900
Hey! You're gonna run?

1221
01:13:54.080 --> 01:13:56.200
I'm not gonna run away from all this.

1222
01:13:56.720 --> 01:13:57.700
All these memories.

1223
01:13:58.520 --> 01:14:00.680
Humans are so attached to each other.

1224
01:14:01.320 --> 01:14:05.100
To their fates, to the alien experiments they've stolen from humans.

1225
01:14:07.220 --> 01:14:08.020
We got to go!

1226
01:14:13.200 --> 01:14:14.400
Attachment means...

1227
01:14:14.400 --> 01:14:15.220
You care.

1228
01:14:18.960 --> 01:14:19.560
Huh?

1229
01:14:20.520 --> 01:14:20.840
Nemo!

1230
01:14:22.260 --> 01:14:23.220
Stop now!

1231
01:14:23.660 --> 01:14:28.060
Caring causes people to make very stupid decisions.

1232
01:14:30.280 --> 01:14:32.060
Who is Mei Mei and Pei Pei?

1233
01:14:33.920 --> 01:14:35.920
That's Mama and Papa's room.

1234
01:14:36.240 --> 01:14:37.880
Oh, that makes a lot more sense.

1235
01:14:42.540 --> 01:14:44.300
Stop it, or else!

1236
01:14:44.640 --> 01:14:45.520
Or else what?

1237
01:14:49.560 --> 01:14:51.460
What are you gonna do?

1238
01:14:52.660 --> 01:14:55.820
There he is!

1239
01:15:12.440 --> 01:15:16.040
I'm sorry.

1240
01:15:16.040 --> 01:15:19.840
My eye! My eye!

1241
01:15:20.020 --> 01:15:20.520
My eye!

1242
01:15:21.280 --> 01:15:22.760
Why would you do this?

1243
01:15:24.040 --> 01:15:25.480
Hey, stop it!

1244
01:15:26.340 --> 01:15:27.780
I'm only trying to help!

1245
01:15:31.800 --> 01:15:34.120
626, playtime is over.

1246
01:15:47.160 --> 01:15:47.700
Oh!

1247
01:15:55.920 --> 01:15:57.440
Okay, okay, okay.

1248
01:15:57.960 --> 01:15:59.080
What's the plan, 626?

1249
01:15:59.600 --> 01:16:00.820
Say you escape the Federation.

1250
01:16:01.380 --> 01:16:03.080
You think you're gonna just stay here with her?

1251
01:16:03.480 --> 01:16:05.500
Live happily ever after on Earth?

1252
01:16:06.020 --> 01:16:08.840
You're built to destroy 626, and you have!

1253
01:16:09.780 --> 01:16:11.720
Look what's happened since you got here.

1254
01:16:12.120 --> 01:16:13.620
Her family is falling apart.

1255
01:16:14.220 --> 01:16:15.240
Let's just be honest.

1256
01:16:15.240 --> 01:16:18.740
The only reason you picked her at that animal shelter

1257
01:16:19.260 --> 01:16:21.280
was for your own protection.

1258
01:16:26.280 --> 01:16:28.380
Is that true, 626?

1259
01:16:29.480 --> 01:16:31.260
See, I don't think that's bad.

1260
01:16:31.800 --> 01:16:33.100
I don't think anything you do is bad.

1261
01:16:33.140 --> 01:16:33.820
I think it's genius.

1262
01:16:35.700 --> 01:16:38.440
If you care about this little girl at all,

1263
01:16:39.020 --> 01:16:40.240
you'll leave her here.

1264
01:16:46.399 --> 01:16:46.879
Peach?

1265
01:16:55.169 --> 01:16:57.330
Ah, this is for the best.

1266
01:17:01.050 --> 01:17:02.010
Peach, run!

1267
01:17:12.100 --> 01:17:14.240
David, Manny, meet me back at the house.

1268
01:17:15.060 --> 01:17:16.360
You know, you made the right choice.

1269
01:17:16.660 --> 01:17:18.360
The councilwoman was gonna exile you.

1270
01:17:18.400 --> 01:17:21.260
She was gonna waste all my brilliant science.

1271
01:17:21.860 --> 01:17:23.840
But I'm gonna do something even better.

1272
01:17:25.660 --> 01:17:29.020
And turn you into 627.

1273
01:17:29.700 --> 01:17:29.920
What?

1274
01:17:32.600 --> 01:17:33.120
Milo?

1275
01:17:33.500 --> 01:17:35.420
Milo? Milo?

1276
01:17:35.600 --> 01:17:36.720
I'm gonna check him out.

1277
01:17:36.920 --> 01:17:37.520
What happened?

1278
01:17:37.720 --> 01:17:38.060
I don't know.

1279
01:17:38.700 --> 01:17:39.540
Where's Milo?

1280
01:17:39.760 --> 01:17:41.720
I don't know. She's not here.

1281
01:17:42.700 --> 01:17:44.760
Actually, she's on a ship heading over here.

1282
01:17:44.760 --> 01:17:48.340
Oh, my God!

1283
01:17:48.460 --> 01:17:49.280
Okay, okay.

1284
01:17:49.900 --> 01:17:51.520
That was really impressive, girl.

1285
01:17:51.780 --> 01:17:52.520
Can we go home?

1286
01:17:53.100 --> 01:17:54.500
No, come on. Not that, I guess.

1287
01:17:55.960 --> 01:17:56.360
Actually...

1288
01:17:57.020 --> 01:17:59.060
Agent Cobra Bubbles, CIA.

1289
01:18:00.200 --> 01:18:01.540
Wait, what? CIA?

1290
01:18:01.880 --> 01:18:04.120
Wendell Gleekley from the United Galactic Federation.

1291
01:18:04.260 --> 01:18:05.200
I'm a fellow government worker.

1292
01:18:05.260 --> 01:18:06.060
What are you doing here?

1293
01:18:06.200 --> 01:18:07.600
Now, where is my sister?

1294
01:18:07.720 --> 01:18:09.240
Great news. She's alive and well.

1295
01:18:09.480 --> 01:18:10.880
Well, actually, I don't know if she's well.

1296
01:18:11.020 --> 01:18:12.980
This only tells me the velocity of them moving away from us.

1297
01:18:12.980 --> 01:18:14.720
Enough! I'm taking you out on that.

1298
01:18:14.960 --> 01:18:15.560
Let's go.

1299
01:18:16.420 --> 01:18:18.340
You know, seeing you with that little girl made me realize

1300
01:18:18.920 --> 01:18:21.180
you're not the heartless monster I thought you were.

1301
01:18:21.720 --> 01:18:24.240
But once I remove your capacity for love,

1302
01:18:24.480 --> 01:18:25.680
you'll be perfect.

1303
01:18:26.060 --> 01:18:28.220
And then, with 627 by my side,

1304
01:18:28.280 --> 01:18:31.540
the Councilwoman won't be able to stop me.

1305
01:18:33.020 --> 01:18:35.600
Oh, don't look so sad, 626.

1306
01:18:35.860 --> 01:18:36.660
We have each other.

1307
01:18:37.020 --> 01:18:38.500
I'm your old Hannah,

1308
01:18:38.720 --> 01:18:40.460
just like your friend Lisa used to say.

1309
01:18:40.700 --> 01:18:41.460
Was that her name, Lisa?

1310
01:18:41.460 --> 01:18:42.060
Lily?

1311
01:18:42.520 --> 01:18:42.740
Limo?

1312
01:18:43.100 --> 01:18:43.620
Limo, no.

1313
01:18:43.980 --> 01:18:44.520
What's her name?

1314
01:18:44.740 --> 01:18:45.020
Lilo!

1315
01:18:45.320 --> 01:18:46.420
Oh, yeah, that was it, Lilo.

1316
01:18:46.620 --> 01:18:47.240
Horrible name.

1317
01:18:47.420 --> 01:18:48.380
Let's get off this planet, huh?

1318
01:18:51.340 --> 01:18:52.220
Initiating hyperspeed.

1319
01:18:52.540 --> 01:18:54.380
Ready to launch in two minutes.

1320
01:18:59.020 --> 01:19:00.800
You need to tell me what is going on.

1321
01:19:01.060 --> 01:19:02.160
Where is my sister?

1322
01:19:02.260 --> 01:19:02.800
Not now.

1323
01:19:03.180 --> 01:19:04.780
Priority is reporting this incident

1324
01:19:04.780 --> 01:19:06.500
and getting this thing into custody.

1325
01:19:06.640 --> 01:19:08.900
People need to know what kind of threat they're under.

1326
01:19:09.840 --> 01:19:11.060
I'm not really a threat.

1327
01:19:11.140 --> 01:19:12.700
I'm kind of quite harmless, actually.

1328
01:19:12.980 --> 01:19:14.360
But you don't need to be that concerned.

1329
01:19:14.580 --> 01:19:16.160
This is actually my first mission in the field.

1330
01:19:17.080 --> 01:19:17.720
Wait, wait.

1331
01:19:18.480 --> 01:19:19.980
Aren't you supposed to protect us?

1332
01:19:21.200 --> 01:19:24.000
I took an oath to protect the American people.

1333
01:19:24.460 --> 01:19:24.760
Hey!

1334
01:19:25.260 --> 01:19:26.460
What do you think we are?

1335
01:19:27.320 --> 01:19:28.720
Cobra, you were right.

1336
01:19:29.220 --> 01:19:30.180
The lab was open again

1337
01:19:30.180 --> 01:19:31.600
and we've never seen anything like this.

1338
01:19:33.960 --> 01:19:34.400
Please.

1339
01:19:35.320 --> 01:19:37.160
There is something big at play here.

1340
01:19:37.160 --> 01:19:38.740
Have you found any additional evidence?

1341
01:19:42.040 --> 01:19:43.020
She's my sister.

1342
01:19:43.280 --> 01:19:44.660
He's the only one who can help.

1343
01:19:50.020 --> 01:19:51.480
Also, I took off your bracelets.

1344
01:19:51.720 --> 01:19:52.480
They were uncomfortable.

1345
01:19:56.000 --> 01:19:57.660
Yeah, it just comes down to having a vision.

1346
01:19:58.280 --> 01:19:59.620
That's all science is.

1347
01:20:00.200 --> 01:20:03.080
It's the ability to see what others can't.

1348
01:20:03.380 --> 01:20:05.300
And I'm guilty of that.

1349
01:20:05.300 --> 01:20:07.380
The Grand Councilwoman, for example.

1350
01:20:08.020 --> 01:20:09.720
She couldn't see the future

1351
01:20:09.720 --> 01:20:11.860
if it was standing right in front of her.

1352
01:20:12.500 --> 01:20:14.040
I wouldn't say that to her face.

1353
01:20:19.100 --> 01:20:19.580
Hey!

1354
01:20:19.900 --> 01:20:21.020
What are you doing?

1355
01:20:22.480 --> 01:20:24.120
Hey, 60, please don't touch the wire.

1356
01:20:25.060 --> 01:20:27.420
Hey, do not touch another wire.

1357
01:20:27.620 --> 01:20:28.040
Please.

1358
01:20:29.440 --> 01:20:30.420
It's really frustrating

1359
01:20:30.980 --> 01:20:32.940
to have this relationship with you

1360
01:20:32.940 --> 01:20:34.540
and I say something and you ignore it.

1361
01:20:34.540 --> 01:20:36.180
When we get back,

1362
01:20:36.520 --> 01:20:37.900
there's going to be some real changes.

1363
01:20:37.980 --> 01:20:39.740
Not so fast, Pizza Face.

1364
01:20:46.320 --> 01:20:46.840
Lisa.

1365
01:20:51.320 --> 01:20:52.620
Let me guess,

1366
01:20:52.640 --> 01:20:53.840
you don't know how to work the spaceship.

1367
01:21:01.620 --> 01:21:02.660
You little...

1368
01:21:06.680 --> 01:21:07.260
What?

1369
01:21:07.440 --> 01:21:08.840
Why do you have party lights?

1370
01:21:09.140 --> 01:21:10.460
Well, that's none of your business.

1371
01:21:10.760 --> 01:21:11.680
Why don't you just admit

1372
01:21:11.680 --> 01:21:12.760
that your little friend

1373
01:21:12.760 --> 01:21:15.320
is a dangerous, freakish monster?

1374
01:21:18.000 --> 01:21:20.660
Also, cute and fluffy.

1375
01:21:22.060 --> 01:21:23.040
Hyper speed.

1376
01:21:23.340 --> 01:21:24.040
Ready for launch.

1377
01:21:34.940 --> 01:21:36.000
Time to go home.

1378
01:21:38.380 --> 01:21:39.180
Hey, hey, hey.

1379
01:21:39.200 --> 01:21:39.780
What are you doing?

1380
01:21:39.960 --> 01:21:41.340
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

1381
01:21:58.670 --> 01:22:01.450
Look, look, look, look, look.

1382
01:22:01.610 --> 01:22:03.250
I had a pretty bad O'Hannah growing up.

1383
01:22:03.370 --> 01:22:04.150
There's not any excuse.

1384
01:22:04.330 --> 01:22:05.250
I just thought I'd give it a little...

1385
01:22:05.250 --> 01:22:06.930
Okay, okay, Tino.

1386
01:22:07.010 --> 01:22:07.770
Okay, okay, okay.

1387
01:22:07.970 --> 01:22:09.670
I suppose that sometimes

1388
01:22:09.670 --> 01:22:11.570
we need second chances.

1389
01:22:21.450 --> 01:22:31.520
They're descending quickly.

1390
01:22:32.140 --> 01:22:33.220
Can you go any faster?

1391
01:22:34.720 --> 01:22:35.840
David, faster.

1392
01:22:36.420 --> 01:22:37.560
You drive me like a grandma.

1393
01:22:55.610 --> 01:22:56.370
Stop.

1394
01:22:57.370 --> 01:22:59.710
There's no way I can't.

1395
01:22:59.910 --> 01:23:00.690
David, stop.

1396
01:23:02.730 --> 01:23:04.150
Stay together.

1397
01:23:08.250 --> 01:23:08.710
Fast.

1398
01:23:09.030 --> 01:23:09.230
Go.

